WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.460
Our case has supporting evidence for the proposed frame and equipment arrangement.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.240
The route review, however, has not established acceptance for one constrained loaded-move

3
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:08.660
segment.

4
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.480
Structural evidence doesn't close that site issue.

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.180
The move remains on hold.

6
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.320
A separate activity may be permitted only if it is independently supported

7
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.540
and doesn't depend on the missing route evidence.

8
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.980
Conditional go must name that activity and its restrictions; it is not

9
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.700
a softer way to approve the move.

10
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.440
Assign the route issue to the responsible site and handling teams, with

11
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.680
a clear closure condition.

12
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.260
If they change the handling configuration or remove equipment for the move,

13
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.420
revisit the affected evidence and post-move verification.

14
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:41.040
Pause and identify the exact record that would permit the decision to

15
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:41.440
change.

16
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.280
The goal is not to accumulate paperwork, but to ensure the requested

17
00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:49.500
activity is supported by the configuration, route and operating conditions that will

18
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.300
actually occur.

